**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery**

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|---------|-------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|
| **G1** | Fulfill Resource Delivery Mission | Ensure that the required resources are collected from storage and delivered to the requesting agent at the specified location. | `;` | **Achieve** | – |
| **G2** | Collect Resources | Perform the collection phase: navigate to storages, request resources, wait for retrieval, handle low battery if needed. | `#` | **Perform** | G1 |
| **G3** | Deliver Resources | Perform the delivery phase: navigate to destination, deliver resources, handle low battery and alerts if necessary. | `#` | **Perform** | G1 |
| **G2.1** | Navigate to Storage | Move to the storage location where resources are located. | `-` | **Perform** | G2 |
| **G2.2** | Request Resources | Send a message to the storage specifying the required resources. | `-` | **Perform** | G2 |
| **G2.3** | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until the requested resources have been retrieved from the storage. | `-` | **Perform** | G2 |
| **G2.4** | Handle Low Battery in Collection | If battery <10 %, return to recharge station and assign mission to another robot. | `-` | **Perform** | G2 |
| **G3.1** | Navigate to Delivery Location | Move to the specified delivery location. | `-` | **Perform** | G3 |
| **G3.2** | Deliver Resource | Transfer the resources to the requesting agent at the destination. | `-` | **Perform** | G3 |
| **G3.3** | Handle Low Battery in Delivery | If battery <30 %, return resource to a checkpoint and assign remaining task to another robot. | `-` | **Perform** | G3 |
| **G3.4** | Trigger Alert on Failure | If failure to return resource to checkpoint, trigger alert and send report to sector manager. | `-` | **Perform** | G3 |

---

### Task Model

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|------------------|
| **AT1** | Navigate to Storage | Move to the storage location where resources are located. | AND | **Storage** | [1,n] |
| **AT2** | Send Request Message | Send a message to the storage specifying the requested resources. | AND | **Storage** | 1 |
| **AT3** | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until the requested resources have been retrieved from the storage. | AND | **Storage** | 1 |
| **AT4** | Navigate to Delivery Location | Move to the specified delivery location. | AND | **Delivery** | 1 |
| **AT5** | Deliver Resource | Transfer the resources to the requesting agent at the destination. | AND | **Delivery** | 1 |
| **AT6** | Return to Recharge Station | Return to the recharge station when battery <10 % during collection. | AND | **Recharge** | 1 |
| **AT7** | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Assign the remaining mission to another robot after low battery. | AND | **Control Center** | 1 |
| **AT8** | Return Resource to Checkpoint | Return the resource to a checkpoint when battery <30 % during delivery. | AND | **Checkpoint** | 1 |
| **AT9** | Trigger Alert | Trigger an alert and send report to sector manager if failure to return resource to checkpoint. | AND | **Control Center** | 1 |

---

### Logical Relationships (Goal ↔ Task)

- **G2** → AT1, AT2, AT3, AT6, AT7 [AND]  
- **G3** → AT4, AT5, AT8, AT7, AT9 [AND]  

The runtime annotations reflect the mission structure:  
* `;` – collection must finish before delivery starts.  
* `#` – within each phase, multiple robots can work in parallel (e.g., several storages).  
* `-` – leaf goals/tasks with no further decomposition.

---

### Justification of Goal Types

| Goal | Type | Reasoning |
|------|------|------------|
| G1 | **Achieve** | The mission succeeds only when the final condition “resources delivered” holds. |
| G2, G3, G2.x, G3.x | **Perform** | Each sub‑goal describes a concrete action that must be executed (navigation, messaging, waiting). |
| – | – | No goal requires only information retrieval; all are action‑oriented. |

---

This goal–task model captures the hierarchical, parallel/serial structure of the multi‑robot resource delivery mission and can be directly mapped to a planner or runtime monitor for the robot fleet.
